WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.374 --> 00:00:03.258
Unit thirteen. Food Security!

2
00:00:04.207 --> 00:00:08.751
Hello, everyone! I'm Doctor Sokha, your school doctor.

3
00:00:08.801 --> 00:00:11.780
Hi, Doctor Sokha! What do we learn today?

4
00:00:11.830 --> 00:00:15.639
Today we learn about Food Security. Let's go!

5
00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:21.507
Food security. Say it with me. Food security!

6
00:00:25.032 --> 00:00:28.565
Hunger. Say it with me. Hunger!

7
00:00:32.088 --> 00:00:36.488
Malnutrition. Say it with me. Malnutrition!

8
00:00:40.023 --> 00:00:43.957
Stunting. Say it with me. Stunting!

9
00:00:47.394 --> 00:00:51.494
Access. Say it with me. Access!

10
00:00:55.038 --> 00:00:59.305
Affordability. Say it with me. Affordability!

11
00:01:02.793 --> 00:01:07.193
Agriculture. Say it with me. Agriculture!

12
00:01:10.654 --> 00:01:14.288
Policy. Say it with me. Policy!

13
00:01:17.788 --> 00:01:29.212
Food security means everyone has access to enough safe, nutritious food. Hunger and malnutrition can cause stunting in children. Affordability, agriculture, and policy all matter.

14
00:01:29.262 --> 00:01:32.380
Now I understand. Thank you, Doctor Sokha!

15
00:01:33.413 --> 00:01:38.646
Look! What's the word?

16
00:01:38.696 --> 00:01:40.070
Malnutrition!

17
00:01:41.321 --> 00:01:46.661
Look! What's the word?

18
00:01:46.711 --> 00:01:47.934
Agriculture!

19
00:01:48.980 --> 00:01:56.464
Did you know? Stunting — being too short for one's age — is a sign of long-term undernutrition in childhood!

20
00:01:56.514 --> 00:01:58.827
Wow! I did not know that!

21
00:01:59.871 --> 00:02:07.840
Think and answer. What causes food insecurity?

22
00:02:07.890 --> 00:02:09.149
Great answer!

23
00:02:10.104 --> 00:02:15.603
Great job today! Stay healthy, and see you next time. Goodbye!

24
00:02:15.653 --> 00:02:18.586
Goodbye, everyone! Stay healthy!

